So that's one thing. The other thing is the content of the title attributes.

When the child board has new posts the "New" thingy links to ?action=unread;board=** while the board name obviously just links to ?board=** yet they both have the same title content, which implies they both do the same thing. I think this is a GUI fail, and it would be better if the child board link always had the total post and topics, and left the "New" count to the "New" thingy title. That way they're not claiming to do the same thing and trying to trick newbies. It'd also save you a ternary in the template, which is not such a bad thing either,
  
